  "articleBody": "When a restraining order is issued, it can feel like a permanent black cloud hanging over you. But the truth is, a restraining order isn't always permanent, although it can certainly feel that way and have long-lasting effects. Typically, an initial temporary restraining order (TRO) is issued to provide immediate protection and lasts for a short period, usually a couple of weeks, until a full court hearing can be held. At that hearing, the judge will decide whether to issue a ",
